; The reciprocal of a pure index view is the view of the reciprocal: a view
; only chooses which element each output coordinate reads (a padding view
; clamps its read, the fill is a select), so taking the reciprocal before or
; after it reads the same value with the same rounding. torch's division by
; a scalar (`x / s`, a VAE resnet's `/ output_scale_factor`) is recorded as
; `x * recip(expand(s))`; with this rule the divisor's reciprocal is also
; the broadcast of a one-element reciprocal, where it was only a full-size
; tensor the size of `x`. One direction: the view's operand gains a
; reciprocal, the view itself is never pushed inside one.
(rule
  ((= ?recip (LogicalRecip (LogicalIndexMapApply ?input ?map ?output_shape))))
  ((union ?recip (LogicalIndexMapApply (LogicalRecip ?input) ?map ?output_shape)))
  :ruleset main_ruleset
  :name "recip/rewrite_view: the reciprocal of a view is the view of the reciprocal"
)
